  "segments": [
    {
      "text": "I don't know how it happens but every single time I sit down to watch something the remote disappears. I swear I just had it. I'll turn on the TV, get comfortable and somehow it's already gone. So there I am lifting up couch cushions, checking under a blanket I haven't moved in hours, looking on the coffee table that's been empty since yesterday. It's as if the thing just vanishes into another dimension. I even start blaming the people I live with. \"Did you move it?\" Even though I know they haven't touched it. Then comes that classic move. I grab my phone turn on the flashlight and go full detective mode wondering how something that small can cause this much chaos. And of course I eventually find it in the dumbest spot possible right next to me hiding under a pillow or worse I've been holding it the entire time. The best part that little rush of victory when I finally find it like I've accomplished something big. I'll sit back down press play and then realize the batteries are dead. It's funny though that tiny remote somehow manages to turn a quiet evening into a full-blown scavenger hunt",
      "start_time": 0.099,
      "end_time": 66.919,
